avanese doughnut, also known in Indonesian as donat jawa, is a traditional doughnut snack, typically savoury, made of cassava instead of potato or flour. This doughnut is quite popular in Javanese cuisine in Java, especially in Central Java, Yogyakarta, and East Java, Indonesia. It is usually served during Javanese occasions, such as wedding parties, wayang shows, ketoprak theater, and Ramadan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-javanese-doughnut"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Javanese_doughnut"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Javanese cuisine","cuisine/javanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Cassava","ingredient/cassava"]]},{"h":"More from Javanese cuisine","links":[["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Getuk goreng","dish/getuk-goreng"],["Megono","dish/megono"],["Nasi ambeng","dish/nasi-ambeng"],["Nasi gandul","dish/nasi-gandul"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/c/cb/Donat_jawa.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Rahmawati Hasanah","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Donat_jawa.jpg"}},"ingredient/piper-sarmentosum":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/piper-sarmentosum","n":"Piper sarmentosum","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Piper sarmentosum (lolot pepper, lolot, wild betel) is a plant in the family Piperaceae used in many Southeast Asian cuisines. The leaves are often confused with betel, but they lack the intense taste of the betel leaves and are significantly smaller."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-piper-sarmentosum"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piper_sarmentosum"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Miang kham","dis